<p>For a faster search, use the pulldown menus to perform exact searches. Each text box can take several entries, separated by commas; a specimen is found if it matches any of them (with "Not equals": none of them). An entry of several words is searched as one phrase: "Santa Cruz" finds Santa Cruz, not every Santa and every Cruz. Specimen, locality and collection codes may also be separated by spaces or line breaks. "Equals" means the whole entry: in the taxon name box, rufa finds the species (and subspecies) named rufa, not pseudorufa, and "Formica rufa" finds that species.</p>
